DITQASM 2.0;
// Qutrit Deutsch-Jozsa, constant oracle, 1 work qutrit.
// q[0] is the work qutrit. q[1] is the oracle ancilla.
// The ancilla is prepared in F^{-1}|1>, an eigenstate of the shift.
// The constant oracle is z three times: Z_3^3 = I.
// The inverse Fourier is h three times. F_3^4 = I, so F_3^3 = F_3^{-1}.
// There is no hdg gate. The ancilla is then returned to |0>, so the
// all-zeros index is the whole state, not a marginal.
qreg q [2][3,3];
x q[1];
h q[1];
h q[1];
h q[1];
h q[0];
z q[0];
z q[0];
z q[0];
h q[0];
h q[0];
h q[0];
h q[1];
x q[1];
x q[1];
